        "summary_cn": "本文利用Rashba-Zeeman-Hubbard模型和Dyson-Gor’kov方程，结合涨落交换近似，研究了反铁磁量子临界区域中d波超导体的超导二极管效应(SDE)。结果表明，电子关联抑制了由退耦电流引起的传统本征SDE，但超电流会非互易地诱发反铁磁序，从而主导临界电流并实现完美二极管效率。该工作揭示了SDE的关联驱动新机制。",
        "abstract_excerpt": "The superconducting diode effect (SDE), characterized by a nonreciprocal critical current in superconductors, has recently been observed in strongly correlated electron systems and near quantum criticality. Here we investigate the SDE in the Rashba-Zeeman-Hubbard model, which captures $d$-wave superconductivity in an antiferromagnetic quantum critical regime. We show that electron correlations suppress the conventional intrinsic SDE arising from depairing currents. More importantly, a supercurrent nonreciprocally induces antiferromagnetic order, which fundamentally governs the critical current",
